# The build context is the whole repository, so what it must not carry is
# everything a build produces. `target/` alone is gigabytes, and sending it
# costs more than the compile it would save: the build has its own cache mount.
target/
target-coverage/
reference/
.git/
# The documentation site's dependency tree and its output, 240 MB of it. These
# arrived under `docs/` when `M45` moved the toolchain beside the pages, and the
# context carried them silently: nothing in the build fails, it is just slower
# for every image anybody builds. The pages themselves stay, because the load
# generator embeds a workload file from `docs/internal/product/perf/`.
docs/node_modules/
docs/dist/
docs/.astro/
